<h2 id="beyond-the-3nf">Beyond the 3NF</h2>

<p>As I anticipated in the beginning, normal forms go way beyond the 3NF, but they’re mostly of academic interest and there’s little to none interest in normal database development to keep this order of normalization. But for the sake of curiosity, let’s anyway have a look to what we can find beyond the 3NF.</p>

<h3 id="boyce-codd-normalization-form">Boyce-Codd Normalization Form</h3>

<p>BCNF is a stricter version of 3NF where every determinant is a candidate key. It ensures that functional dependencies are resolved more rigorously, even in complex scenarios.</p>

<h3 id="fourth-and-fifth-normalization-forms">Fourth and Fifth Normalization Forms</h3>

<p>4th Normalization Form deals with multi-valued dependencies while the 5th Normalization Forms define a standardized way to work with joined tables.</p>

